  28:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *
  29:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * \brief Writes the value to the physical port (data output register), masking
  30:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  and shifting the bits appropriately. 
  31:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *
  32:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * The data output register controls the signal applied to the physical pin in 
  33:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * conjunction with the drive mode parameter. This function avoids changing 
  34:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * other bits in the port by using the appropriate method (read-modify-write or
  35:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * bit banding).
  36:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *
  37:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * <b>Note</b> This function should not be used on a hardware digital output pin 
  38:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * as it is driven by the hardware signal attached to it.
  39:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *
  40:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * \param value
  41:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  Value to write to the component instance.
  42:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *
  43:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * \return 
  44:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  None 
  45:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *
  46:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * \sideeffect
  47:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  If you use read-modify-write operations that are not atomic; the Interrupt 
  48:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  Service Routines (ISR) can cause corruption of this function. An ISR that 
  49:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  interrupts this function and performs writes to the Pins component data 
  50:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  register can cause corrupted port data. To avoid this issue, you should 
  51:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  either use the Per-Pin APIs (primary method) or disable interrupts around 
  52:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  this function.
  53:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *
  54:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** * \funcusage
  55:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *  \snippet SEo_SUT.c usage_SEo_Write
  56:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** *******************************************************************************/
  57:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** void SEo_Write(uint8 value)
  58:Generated_Source\PSoC5/SEo.c **** {
